[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2892235628","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2745#issuecomment-2892235628","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2745","id":2892235628,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86sZANs","user":{"login":"xsuchy","id":85769,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NzY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85769?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy","html_url":"https://github.com/xsuchy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-19T20:51:54Z","updated_at":"2025-05-19T20:51:54Z","body":"Text of the exception:\n```\n                         EXCEPTION NOTICE\n\n1. As a special exception, the copyright holders of this library give\npermission for additional uses of the text contained in this release\nof the library as licensed under the Simple Library Usage License,\napplying either version 1 of the License, or (at your option) any\nlater version of the License as published by the copyright holders of\nversion 1 of the License document.\n\n2. The exception is that you may combine or link a \"work that uses the\nLibrary\" (as defined by the LGPL) with the Library to produce a work\ncontaining portions of the Library in binary form, and distribute that\nwork under terms of your choice, provided that:\n\n  a) You give prominent notice with each copy of the work that the\n  Library is used in it.\n\n  b) If the work during execution displays copyright notices, you must\n  include the copyright notice for the Library among them.\n\n3. If you copy code from files distributed under the terms of the GNU\nGeneral Public License or the GNU Lesser General Public License into a\ncopy of this library, as this license permits, the exception does not\napply to the code that you add in this way.  To avoid misleading\nanyone as to the status of such modified files, you must delete this\nexception notice from such code and/or adjust the licensing conditions\nnotice accordingly.\n\n4. If you write modifications of your own for this library, it is your\nchoice whether to permit this exception to apply to your\nmodifications.  If you do not wish that, you must delete the exception\nnotice from such code and/or adjust the licensing conditions notice\naccordingly.\n```\n\nIt is similar to https://spdx.org/licenses/WxWindows-exception-3.1.html but the differences are not trivial.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2892235628/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/3281809469","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2745#issuecomment-3281809469","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2745","id":3281809469,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE87DnHA9","user":{"login":"Pizza-Ria","id":46799628,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2Nzk5NjI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46799628?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria","html_url":"https://github.com/Pizza-Ria","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-11T16:43:10Z","updated_at":"2025-09-11T16:43:10Z","body":"This seems to hit, at least, 3/4 criteria for an exception.\n\n- The exception is not a stand-alone license.\n- Grants an exception to a license condition\n- Actual, substantial use such that it is likely to be encountered (Fedora).\n\nClause 3 probably doesn't impose additional restrictions ... more of an invalidating condition for the exception ... and a similar clause is in https://spdx.org/licenses/WxWindows-exception-3.1.html.  \n\nI think it may be a little weird to have an exception tied to a specific license (Simple) if we haven't reviewed and assigned an ID to the Simple Library Usage License.  If we aren't giving the base license an ID then I would rather have the license name as a markdown component to make it more generic.  My preference, however, would be to assess the base license before approving an exception to it.  ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/3281809469/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/3528954093","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/li